      "hypotheses": "Self-dual Hermitian lattice Λ over a CM ring of integers, saturated isotropic R, W its rational span, P=Λ∩W⊥, positive h,l with largest size on R at most h and each extension quotient within P of size at least l.",
      "statement": "Rounding P/R→R gives a rational map Φ with residual of Hilbert–Schmidt norm at most j(n−2j)√f d h/(2l). Splitting the saturated orthogonal lattice in Λ and subtracting the adjoint gives a lattice-preserving nilpotent endomorphism Y₀ which agrees with Φ on P.",
