      "hypotheses": "Use the orthogonal majorant frames, the rank identity dim W⊥=n−j and h/l≤u. The congruence level g is positive.",
      "statement": "The two off-diagonal blocks have equal squared Hilbert–Schmidt norm and disjoint supports. This gives a real central remainder and first covering radius r₁≤n²√f d u/(8√2) in the sense that this value is an upper bound for the displacement. Rescaling to level g costs at most n²√f g d u/(4√2).",
